A drop breaks the foreign key of a WITHOUT ROWID table's rows. Such a row
has no rowid, so the error names its table alone.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE course (menu_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES menu (id), name TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (menu_id, name)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');
INSERT INTO course VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 table menu
CREATE TABLE course (menu_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES menu (id), name TEXT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (menu_id, name)) STRICT, WITHOUT ROWID;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 1 step
  table `menu`: dropped on purpose
    DROP TABLE "menu"

== error
migrating test.db: rows that would break a foreign key: 1; a row of course names no menu
